title: "Google Ads Character Counter & Ad Preview | DigitalFadi"
description: "Free Google Ads character counter. Check headline and description limits live, spot duplicates, and preview your responsive search ad on desktop and mobile."
faqs:
  - q: "What are the Google Ads character limits?"
    a: "Headlines are 30 characters each and you can add up to 15. Descriptions are 90 characters each and you can add up to 4. Path fields are 15 characters each. Spaces and punctuation count towards the limit."
  - q: "How many headlines should a responsive search ad have?"
    a: "Google allows 15 and rewards using most of them, because more combinations give the system more to test. Aim for at least 8 to 10 genuinely different headlines rather than 15 variations of the same sentence."
  - q: "Does this tool send my ad copy anywhere?"
    a: "No. Everything runs in your browser. Your headlines are saved in this browser so they are still there when you come back, but nothing is ever uploaded or sent to any server, including mine. The Clear button removes the saved copy."
  - q: "Is my work saved if I close the tab?"
    a: "Yes. The tool keeps your headlines and descriptions in this browser, so they are still there when you come back on the same device. It is not an account and nothing is sent anywhere. Use Clear to wipe it."
  - q: "Why does my headline get cut off in the preview?"
    a: "Google shows up to three headlines joined by vertical bars, and the full set rarely fits, especially on mobile. The preview shows roughly what Google displays so you can check your most important headline still reads properly when the others are truncated."
